{"reviews":[{"id":"B0105WF7NC-0","r":5.0,"t":"Learn how to use products you order before giving a bad review.","x":"I hate it so much when people give companies on here bad reviews because they're too ignorant to understand how to use a product. I have been using these for years and I love them so much. They file and buff my nails with no issues. I don't know what these other people are doing that they're making themselves bleed or leaving their nails rough. Obviously they don't know how to use it. If you don't know how to use something, google it, YouTube it, or go to the salon and let them do it. How rough ","h":103,"v":1,"d":"Jul 2017"},{"id":"B0105WF7NC-1","r":5.0,"t":"While several people seemed to review this item as \"too ...","x":"While several people seemed to review this item as &#34;too harsh&#34; i think it works  perfectly and those who may have written such reviews do not know how to use the product or that it is mainly for the use on acrylics, not your regular nails!","h":20,"v":1,"d":"Mar 2018"},{"id":"B0105WF7NC-2","r":5.0,"t":"Great product. Will purchase again.","x":"Great professional quality product. Will purchase again! Delivered on time in good condition!","h":7,"v":1,"d":"Jul 2018"},{"id":"B0105WF7NC-3","r":1.0,"t":"Don't bother","x":"Even if these were free they still wouldn't be worth the price. These blocks are so hard, they don't form to the nail at all. The grit us barely stuck on and flies everywhere with every swipe. You have to use at least 2 full sides of the block for each nail just to buff it, because all of the grit comes off before you smooth half the nail. It's annoying, aggravating, huge waste of time and embarrassing to use in front of a client.","h":5,"v":1,"d":"May 2018"},{"id":"B0105WF7NC-4","r":5.0,"t":"they're great for roughing up gel polish for removal and after ...","x":"Didn't realize how course they were going to be initially, but I used them on the areas on the bottom of my toes where the foot file can't reach. Then once the soften up, they're great for roughing up gel polish for removal and after that, for buffing the nail. So you get a lot of use out of them!","h":4,"v":1,"d":"Jun 2016"},{"id":"B0105WF7NC-5","r":5.0,"t":"but they work great and look just as described","x":"I don't know why I ordered 10 of these, but they work great and look just as described.","h":4,"v":1,"d":"Jan 2018"},{"id":"B0105WF7NC-6","r":1.0,"t":"Possibly I misunderstood their intent. The grit on these ...","x":"Possibly I misunderstood their intent.  The grit on these blocks are for horse hooves maybe.  No way a human could use these -- well maybe if you had really really gruff heels -- these are even harder than pumice stone.  I gave the package to my husband to use as sand paper","h":3,"v":1,"d":"Jul 2016"},{"id":"B0105WF7NC-7","r":5.0,"t":"Great value","x":"These are course so they last! If you don\u2019t know how to use these you will hurt yourself! I\u2019m not a professional nail tech by any means so it did take me afew tried to figure out how to use these with a light hand. I use these for dip. Would recommend.","h":3,"v":1,"d":"Jun 2019"},{"id":"B0105WF7NC-8","r":1.0,"t":"very rough","x":"I have been getting my nails done for over 2 decades and also do my own buffing/painting.  These are NOT buffers they are very heavy more like sand paper and will leave marks on your nails.","h":3,"v":1,"d":"May 2019"},{"id":"B0105WF7NC-9","r":1.0,"t":"Very poor quality","x":"Very cheaply made.  The grit flies off when using which makes is fairly worthless in shaping or filing your nails.","h":3,"v":1,"d":"Dec 2017"},{"id":"B0105WF7NC-10","r":1.0,"t":"Extra coarse, too rough for any usage but on rough heels.","x":"Extra coarse on both sides, which I didn't expect. I was disappointed with the fact that it is too coarse to use on anything except rough heels. Don't buy this product for your nails, you won't be able to use it.","h":2,"v":1,"d":"Mar 2017"},{"id":"B0105WF7NC-11","r":5.0,"t":"Perfect for my nails","x":"I really like these files for doing my nails. This is my final step before painting then. I love these because they make your nail bed so soft and take ball polish off to.","h":2,"v":1,"d":"Dec 2018"},{"id":"B0105WF7NC-12","r":5.0,"t":"Great buffers","x":"I like that I can get 10 at a time, I  go through a lot of buffers. These are great quality for the price.","h":2,"v":1,"d":"Jan 2019"},{"id":"B0105WF7NC-13","r":5.0,"t":"Very useful","x":"More coarse then I expected, but i like them!!! Great value for the price.","h":2,"v":1,"d":"Aug 2018"},{"id":"B0105WF7NC-14","r":5.0,"t":"Great but coarse.","x":"Love these buffers but let me tell you they are coarse.","h":2,"v":1,"d":"Aug 2017"},{"id":"B0105WF7NC-15","r":5.0,"t":"Nice product","x":"just want expected, happy to purchase again.","h":2,"v":1,"d":"Sep 2017"},{"id":"B0105WF7NC-16","r":4.0,"t":"Four Stars","x":"Exactly as advertised.  Rough grit, cheap.","h":2,"v":1,"d":"Dec 2016"},{"id":"B0105WF7NC-17","r":5.0,"t":"Super fast shipping!","x":"These are great. I\u2019m a nail tech and for those of you complaining that they are too course, you need to PREP them before use The same way you\u2019d prep knives. There are finer grit buffers that are ideal for natural nails. These are used best for toes or to help remove gel or buff acrylic.","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Jan 2019"},{"id":"B0105WF7NC-18","r":3.0,"t":"Great but Souter","x":"I do use these to take a lot off the dip Powder when It\u2019s thick or I\u2019m just redoing them to look better. These def do the job but are very course and I have def ate up my cuticles and around my nails with these ! So they\u2019re great but can defiantly take the skin off your fingers","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Aug 2018"},{"id":"B0105WF7NC-19","r":1.0,"t":"These are not at all like the previous buffer blocks I have purchased","x":"These are not at all like the previous buffer blocks I have purchased.  They are VERY course.  They would even be course for acrylic nails.","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Mar 2017"},{"id":"B0105WF7NC-20","r":5.0,"t":"buffer blocks","x":"a good buy for me.  i was just buying a couple every time i needed them from sally.  now to buy them like this is a great deal.","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Mar 2019"},{"id":"B0105WF7NC-21","r":5.0,"t":"Durability","x":"These are the best. I have purchased some at walmart and they are nothing compared to these Purple one.","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Aug 2019"},{"id":"B0105WF7NC-22","r":5.0,"t":"Very nice!","x":"I use these to buff my clients gel overlays and extensions. Works like a charm !","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Mar 2019"},{"id":"B0105WF7NC-23","r":3.0,"t":"Very coarse texture","x":"This was not really what I was looking for. It is ok for a coarse buffer.","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Feb 2017"},{"id":"B0105WF7NC-24","r":5.0,"t":"By in bulk - worth it.","x":"I didn't need so many, but they work great on thick nails.","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Apr 2017"}],"emb":"","summary":{"claims":[{"text":"Many reviewers find the blocks too coarse or rough, saying they are harsher than expected and unsuitable for regular nails.","cites":[4,7,9,11,14,15]},{"text":"Several reviewers say the product works well and they are satisfied with its performance.","cites":[1,2,3,5,6,12,13]},{"text":"Some reviewers note the grit comes off or flies off during use, calling the quality poor.","cites":[4,10]},{"text":"Multiple reviewers describe the product as good value for the price.","cites":[8,13,14]},{"text":"Some reviewers say the product requires knowing how to use it with a light hand, and that misuse causes problems.","cites":[1,2,8]}]},"qa":[]}